, "visibility": "public", "forks": 1828, "open_issues": 22, "watchers": 428, "default_branch": "main", "permissions": {"admin": false, "maintain": false, "push": false, "triage": false, "pull": true}}, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/PX4/PX4-user_guide/pulls/1810", "html_url": "https://github.com/PX4/PX4-user_guide/pull/1810", "diff_url": "https://github.com/PX4/PX4-user_guide/pull/1810.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/PX4/PX4-user_guide/pull/1810.patch", "merged_at": "2022-07-28T03:38:37Z"}, "body": "This PR updates the \"Follow Me\" documentation, with the latest (and ongoing) [refactor of the follow target](https://github.com/PX4/PX4-Autopilot/pull/19260) flight mode.\r\n\r\n* https://docs.px4.io/master/en/flight_modes/follow_me.html\r\n\r\nMajor changes are\r\n1. Add new parameter added (NAV_FT_ALT_M, altitude mode)\r\n2. Edit drone behaviour, since the logic has changed\r\n\r\nTODOs\r\n- [x] Add description on how 'follow side' is configured, maybe a diagram.\r\n- [x] New beautiful video on the improved status of the Follow Me feature\r\n- [ ] Add how the drone would behave, in GIF or Diagram, giving a sense on how altitude, orientation and distance will come into effect. (SUPER important!!)\r\n\r\nOpen Questions\r\n1. Should it be named \"Follow Me\" or \"Follow Target\"? It has been renamed to the Follow Target on the refactor, but follow me is more 'user friendly'\r\n2. How are german / korean / japense, etc language translations supported? If there's no change, do they just copy the english document? @hamishwillee ", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/PX4/PX4-user_guide/issues/1810/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/PX4/PX4-user_guide/issues/1810/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null}}, "event": "cross-referenced"}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repo